  "details": "I joined a \"group public\" world through a friend, but it seems that because I had previously blocked the creator of this world, he kicked me out. This made me feel very upset, and what’s even more shocking is that I have no way of knowing who kicked me out. The \"group public\" world creation method has a flaw, as it allows the creator to hide their identity. I suggest adding a feature to display the name of the creator of the \"group public\" world.\n\nFeature implementation: On the details page of the world, when the cursor hovers over the group name, it should display the name of the player who created the world.\n\nAdding this feature to display the name of the creator of a \"group public\" world when hovering over the group name would bring several benefits to all players:\n\n1.Transparency and Accountability\n\nPlayers will know who is responsible for creating and managing the world, making the process more transparent. This accountability can discourage misuse, such as kicking players without valid reasons, and foster a sense of fairness.\n\n2.Improved Player Trust\n\nKnowing the creator's identity can help players feel more secure when joining \"group public\" worlds, as they can better understand who they are interacting with and whether the creator aligns with their preferences or expectations.\n\n3.Enhanced Social Interaction\n\nDisplaying the creator's name allows players to directly recognize and engage with the creator, fostering opportunities for collaboration, networking, or simply building social connections within the community.",
